  <item nodeId="node-21">
    <command xml:space="preserve">nw</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You loop under a tree branch and head northwest, but before you get very far, you hear something whap against the Librum door behind you.  Something almost escaped from in there.&#x000A;&#x000A;Royal Gardens&#x000A;The Royal Gardens is the most lavishly opulent and sensuous entrance to any aerie you've seen in your life.  Trees, vines, and flowers of every variety spring up from everywhere, each seemingly placed in the exactly appropriate spot.  The landing cradle next to the garden door to the Royal Quarters themselves is nestled between gracious arcs of poplar trunks, each bedecked with shaded and inviting roosts.  Which, as you know from your childhood days swooping and laughing through these gardens, invariably contain at least eight guards.  Probably ten or more today.&#x000A;&#x000A;From here, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.  The Great Hall is to the south, and the Librum to the southeast.  The door to the very-guarded Royal Quarters is to the north.&#x000A;&#x000A;You dodge and weave and almost get away from your pursuers, but when "down" always points straight at you, even when they can't see you, they always know where you are.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You loop under a tree branch and head northwest, but before you get very far, you hear something whap against the Librum door behind you.  Something almost escaped from in there.&#x000A;&#x000A;Royal Gardens&#x000A;The Royal Gardens is the most lavishly opulent and sensuous entrance to any aerie you've seen in your life.  Trees, vines, and flowers of every variety spring up from everywhere, each seemingly placed in the exactly appropriate spot.  The landing cradle next to the garden door to the Royal Quarters themselves is nestled between gracious arcs of poplar trunks, each bedecked with shaded and inviting roosts.  Which, as you know from your childhood days swooping and laughing through these gardens, invariably contain at least eight guards.  Probably ten or more today.&#x000A;&#x000A;From here, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.  The Great Hall is to the south, and the Librum to the southeast.  The door to the very-guarded Royal Quarters is to the north.&#x000A;&#x000A;You dodge and weave and almost get away from your pursuers, but when "down" always points straight at you, even when they can't see you, they always know where you are.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-22"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-22">
    <command xml:space="preserve">open purple</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You take a deep breath.  If you're going to get past any of the doors here, this is the only way.&#x000A;&#x000A;You open the purple capsa of opening, revealing a scroll of rezrov.&#x000A;&#x000A;As you open the purple capsa, an almost-palpable wave of force emanates from it, as the power of the revealed scroll of rezrov is released.&#x000A;&#x000A;The garden door clicks as it unlocks!&#x000A;The magic of the red capsa of hasten prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The double doors of the great hall fly open!&#x000A;The garden door flies open!&#x000A;The straps and buckles on your rucksack fly open and it falls!&#x000A;Fortunately, it hovers in midair due to the scroll of down, so you're able to immediately grab it again.&#x000A;&#x000A;The guards charge, but you manage to evade their uncoordinated attack.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You take a deep breath.  If you're going to get past any of the doors here, this is the only way.&#x000A;&#x000A;You open the purple capsa of opening, revealing a scroll of rezrov.&#x000A;&#x000A;As you open the purple capsa, an almost-palpable wave of force emanates from it, as the power of the revealed scroll of rezrov is released.&#x000A;&#x000A;The garden door clicks as it unlocks!&#x000A;The magic of the red capsa of hasten prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The double doors of the great hall fly open!&#x000A;The garden door flies open!&#x000A;The straps and buckles on your rucksack fly open and it falls!&#x000A;Fortunately, it hovers in midair due to the scroll of down, so you're able to immediately grab it again.&#x000A;&#x000A;The guards charge, but you manage to evade their uncoordinated attack.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-23"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-23">
    <command xml:space="preserve">se</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A black capsa flies through the doors of the Librum, up towards you!&#x000A;&#x000A;You dodge and weave and almost get away from your pursuers, but when "down" always points straight at you, even when they can't see you, they always know where you are.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A black capsa flies through the doors of the Librum, up towards you!&#x000A;&#x000A;You dodge and weave and almost get away from your pursuers, but when "down" always points straight at you, even when they can't see you, they always know where you are.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-24"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-24">
    <command xml:space="preserve">w</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;The black capsa follows you from Librum Landing Cradle, spiraling towards the gold capsa of down.&#x000A;Suddenly the great wooden bar that had been holding the Great Hall doors closed gets dislodged, and flies at you!  You turn and weave, managing to keep it from hitting you.  The Raven Guard fall back as the spinning bar careens through the air!&#x000A;&#x000A;You dodge and weave and almost get away from your pursuers, but when "down" always points straight at you, even when they can't see you, they always know where you are.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;The black capsa follows you from Librum Landing Cradle, spiraling towards the gold capsa of down.&#x000A;Suddenly the great wooden bar that had been holding the Great Hall doors closed gets dislodged, and flies at you!  You turn and weave, managing to keep it from hitting you.  The Raven Guard fall back as the spinning bar careens through the air!&#x000A;&#x000A;You dodge and weave and almost get away from your pursuers, but when "down" always points straight at you, even when they can't see you, they always know where you are.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-25"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-25">
    <command xml:space="preserve">n</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Royal Gardens&#x000A;The Royal Gardens is the most lavishly opulent and sensuous entrance to any aerie you've seen in your life.  Trees, vines, and flowers of every variety spring up from everywhere, each seemingly placed in the exactly appropriate spot.  The landing cradle next to the garden door to the Royal Quarters themselves is nestled between gracious arcs of poplar trunks, each bedecked with shaded and inviting roosts.  Which, as you know from your childhood days swooping and laughing through these gardens, invariably contain at least eight guards.  Probably ten or more today.&#x000A;&#x000A;From here, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.  The Great Hall is to the south, and the Librum to the southeast.  The door to the very-guarded Royal Quarters is to the north.&#x000A;&#x000A;The wooden bar follows you from Great Hall Landing Cradle, spiraling towards the gold capsa of down.&#x000A;The black capsa follows you from Great Hall Landing Cradle, spiraling towards the gold capsa of down.&#x000A;&#x000A;You dodge and weave and almost get away from your pursuers, but when "down" always points straight at you, even when they can't see you, they always know where you are.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
