  <item nodeId="node-35">
    <command xml:space="preserve">z</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You circle evasively, trying to avoid the Raven Guard.&#x000A;&#x000A;Your luck runs out as you dodge the wrong way, and the wooden bar smacks into your side.  You get the wind knocked out of you, the bar stops blocking the guard from following, and in an instant, they've swarmed you, bearing down on you from all directions.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;    *** You have been captured. ***&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;Would you like to RESTART, RESTORE a saved game, QUIT, or UNDO the last command?&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You circle evasively, trying to avoid the Raven Guard.&#x000A;&#x000A;Your luck runs out as you dodge the wrong way, and the wooden bar smacks into your side.  You get the wind knocked out of you, the bar stops blocking the guard from following, and in an instant, they've swarmed you, bearing down on you from all directions.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;    *** You have been captured. ***&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;Would you like to RESTART, RESTORE a saved game, QUIT, or UNDO the last command?&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-36"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-36">
    <command xml:space="preserve">undo</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;[Previous turn undone.]&#x000A;&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;[Previous turn undone.]&#x000A;&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-37"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-37">
    <command xml:space="preserve">get bar</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Taken.&#x000A;&#x000A;The guards charge, but you manage to evade their uncoordinated attack.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Taken.&#x000A;&#x000A;The guards charge, but you manage to evade their uncoordinated attack.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
