      <child nodeId="node-38"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-38">
    <command xml:space="preserve">put bar in rucksack</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The wooden bar is much to large to fit in the rucksack.&#x000A;&#x000A;Two guards snap at you, and while both touch nothing but feathers, a third slashes you with his silvered talons.  They're about to overwhelm you.&#x000A;&#x000A;Your wound continues to lightly bleed.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">The wooden bar is much to large to fit in the rucksack.&#x000A;&#x000A;Two guards snap at you, and while both touch nothing but feathers, a third slashes you with his silvered talons.  They're about to overwhelm you.&#x000A;&#x000A;Your wound continues to lightly bleed.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-39"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-39">
    <command xml:space="preserve">d</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You descend towards the forest floor, though it feels like you're flying upwards, against the pull of the scroll of down.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the Forest&#x000A;The trees below the Royal Aerie grow more closely together than in the rest of the forest, and include a wider variety, so that differently-colored woods could be incorporated into the buildings above.  This makes it harder to navigate down here--or it would if you weren't so amazing at navigation.&#x000A;&#x000A;Even through the mist, your sharp eyes spot a fine net, stretched between the trees.  It seems to be set to prevent anyone from coming up from the forest below.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Raven Guard pursues you determinedly through the thin mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You descend towards the forest floor, though it feels like you're flying upwards, against the pull of the scroll of down.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the Forest&#x000A;The trees below the Royal Aerie grow more closely together than in the rest of the forest, and include a wider variety, so that differently-colored woods could be incorporated into the buildings above.  This makes it harder to navigate down here--or it would if you weren't so amazing at navigation.&#x000A;&#x000A;Even through the mist, your sharp eyes spot a fine net, stretched between the trees.  It seems to be set to prevent anyone from coming up from the forest below.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Raven Guard pursues you determinedly through the thin mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-40"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-40">
    <command xml:space="preserve">close gold</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You close the gold capsa of down.&#x000A;&#x000A;You twist and right yourself as "down" returns to its normal state.  The Raven Guards struggle to right themselves again, and take a moment to recover.&#x000A;The wooden bar is ripped from your talons and falls!&#x000A;&#x000A;Dropped.&#x000A;&#x000A;The guards charge, but you manage to evade their uncoordinated attack.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You close the gold capsa of down.&#x000A;&#x000A;You twist and right yourself as "down" returns to its normal state.  The Raven Guards struggle to right themselves again, and take a moment to recover.&#x000A;The wooden bar is ripped from your talons and falls!&#x000A;&#x000A;Dropped.&#x000A;&#x000A;The guards charge, but you manage to evade their uncoordinated attack.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-41"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-41">
    <command xml:space="preserve">u</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You gracefully flit between the trees back up above the canopy.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Raven Guard pursues you determinedly through the thin mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You gracefully flit between the trees back up above the canopy.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Raven Guard pursues you determinedly through the thin mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-42"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-42">
    <command xml:space="preserve">u</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Raven Guard pursues you determinedly through the thin mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Raven Guard pursues you determinedly through the thin mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-43"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-43">
    <command xml:space="preserve">d</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You tuck in your wings and dive down towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;Your speed puts more distance between you and your pursuers, but it's not quite fast enough, or the mist isn't thick enough, or both, and your pursuers manage to keep you in sight.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You tuck in your wings and dive down towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;Your speed puts more distance between you and your pursuers, but it's not quite fast enough, or the mist isn't thick enough, or both, and your pursuers manage to keep you in sight.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-44"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-44">
    <command xml:space="preserve">d</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the Forest&#x000A;The trees below the Royal Aerie grow more closely together than in the rest of the forest, and include a wider variety, so that differently-colored woods could be incorporated into the buildings above.  This makes it harder to navigate down here--or it would if you weren't so amazing at navigation.&#x000A;&#x000A;Even through the mist, your sharp eyes spot a fine net, stretched between the trees.  It seems to be set to prevent anyone from coming up from the forest below.&#x000A;&#x000A;You can also see a wooden bar here.&#x000A;&#x000A;You expertly twist at breakneck speeds, weaving through three Ash trunks, over a branch, and around and behind a Redwood, where you halt, twist, and dive straight down the trunk, out of view of any stray Raven.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Raven's frustrated caws echo in the thin mist.  In time, the woodpeckers cease their drumming, and the cawing fades as well.  Protocol would dictate that they return to guarding priority items.  If there were any reserves left, they would be called up, but the Red Plague has affected the Raven Guard as sorely as your own community.&#x000A;&#x000A;You plot a now-unseen course back to the familiar currents above the Aerie to ponder your next move.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;                                                              *    *    *</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">In the Forest&#x000A;The trees below the Royal Aerie grow more closely together than in the rest of the forest, and include a wider variety, so that differently-colored woods could be incorporated into the buildings above.  This makes it harder to navigate down here--or it would if you weren't so amazing at navigation.&#x000A;&#x000A;Even through the mist, your sharp eyes spot a fine net, stretched between the trees.  It seems to be set to prevent anyone from coming up from the forest below.&#x000A;&#x000A;You can also see a wooden bar here.&#x000A;&#x000A;You expertly twist at breakneck speeds, weaving through three Ash trunks, over a branch, and around and behind a Redwood, where you halt, twist, and dive straight down the trunk, out of view of any stray Raven.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Raven's frustrated caws echo in the thin mist.  In time, the woodpeckers cease their drumming, and the cawing fades as well.  Protocol would dictate that they return to guarding priority items.  If there were any reserves left, they would be called up, but the Red Plague has affected the Raven Guard as sorely as your own community.&#x000A;&#x000A;You plot a now-unseen course back to the familiar currents above the Aerie to ponder your next move.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;                                                              *    *    *</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-45"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-45">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You wait, expectantly.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You wait, expectantly.</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-46"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-46">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Silently, your cell door unlocks, then swings open.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Silently, your cell door unlocks, then swings open.</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-47"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-47">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Well above your cell, you sense quiste, rezrov, and rudenj settle in their movements until they make lazy circles, high above the Aerie.  Oh, and igram is with them.  Resourceful girl.  Taclor remains in place, quiet.&#x000A;&#x000A;It is time.&#x000A;&#x000A;Forgotten Brig&#x000A;A small but cosy cell, grown with austerity but basic comfort in mind.  Your now-open cell door leads west.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Well above your cell, you sense quiste, rezrov, and rudenj settle in their movements until they make lazy circles, high above the Aerie.  Oh, and igram is with them.  Resourceful girl.  Taclor remains in place, quiet.&#x000A;&#x000A;It is time.&#x000A;&#x000A;Forgotten Brig&#x000A;A small but cosy cell, grown with austerity but basic comfort in mind.  Your now-open cell door leads west.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-48"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-48">
    <command xml:space="preserve">w</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Disused Hallway&#x000A;The only time you ever saw anyone in this hallway was when Georg came to give you your meals, or clean the cell.  The living walls, still elegantly patterned, even here, self-replenish, and the floor carries away shed bark through the grate.  It leads west into the living area, and your old cell door leads east.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Disused Hallway&#x000A;The only time you ever saw anyone in this hallway was when Georg came to give you your meals, or clean the cell.  The living walls, still elegantly patterned, even here, self-replenish, and the floor carries away shed bark through the grate.  It leads west into the living area, and your old cell door leads east.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-49"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-49">
    <command xml:space="preserve">in</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flatten yourself to the floor and, hearing your bones creak, roll into the space behind the grate.  Using your minimal throck ability, you whisper a song to the veins of this place: "I am extra.  I am not needed.  Take me from this place, which will renew itself through my absence."&#x000A;&#x000A;After a few moments, you feel an undulation in the slick rippled floor beneath you, and you are compressed even further, as its peristalsis slides you slowly, and then more rapidly, away from your only home for the last ten years.  Then with a sudden &gt;plop&lt;, you're ejected into space.&#x000A;&#x000A;You try to spread your wings, but your reaction time is not what it was, and you hit wirey netting before fully stopping yourself.&#x000A;&#x000A;No matter.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the Forest&#x000A;The tightly-growing trees and thick fog surround you tightly.  It would be oppressive, but for the echo of the Throckwright song you can just sense, flowing through the veins of these trees still.  That, and the fact that you've been confined to a single room for a decade, so any contrast is welcome.&#x000A;&#x000A;The net that caught you stretches in every direction, preventing both entrance to and egress from the rest of the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;You can also see a wooden bar here.&#x000A;&#x000A;A thick mist surrounds you, summoned by your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You flatten yourself to the floor and, hearing your bones creak, roll into the space behind the grate.  Using your minimal throck ability, you whisper a song to the veins of this place: "I am extra.  I am not needed.  Take me from this place, which will renew itself through my absence."&#x000A;&#x000A;After a few moments, you feel an undulation in the slick rippled floor beneath you, and you are compressed even further, as its peristalsis slides you slowly, and then more rapidly, away from your only home for the last ten years.  Then with a sudden &gt;plop&lt;, you're ejected into space.&#x000A;&#x000A;You try to spread your wings, but your reaction time is not what it was, and you hit wirey netting before fully stopping yourself.&#x000A;&#x000A;No matter.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the Forest&#x000A;The tightly-growing trees and thick fog surround you tightly.  It would be oppressive, but for the echo of the Throckwright song you can just sense, flowing through the veins of these trees still.  That, and the fact that you've been confined to a single room for a decade, so any contrast is welcome.&#x000A;&#x000A;The net that caught you stretches in every direction, preventing both entrance to and egress from the rest of the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;You can also see a wooden bar here.&#x000A;&#x000A;A thick mist surrounds you, summoned by your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-50"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-50">
    <command xml:space="preserve">u</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Forcing your tired wings to flap again, you rise above the forest floor, past the level of your cell, up above the canopy.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall was the first you ever saw of this Aerie, when you arrived ten years ago in the entourage of the Waterfowl delegation.  You were impressed by the huge double doors of the Great Hall, large enough to comfortably accomodate even the largest of your distant kin, and the diversity of clans here to meet you was equally fascinating.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum is to the east, the doors to the Great Hall are west, and if your wings are up for it, you could return to the skies and fly up (where Constance circles) or back down to the forest floor.&#x000A;&#x000A;A thick mist surrounds you, summoned by your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Forcing your tired wings to flap again, you rise above the forest floor, past the level of your cell, up above the canopy.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall was the first you ever saw of this Aerie, when you arrived ten years ago in the entourage of the Waterfowl delegation.  You were impressed by the huge double doors of the Great Hall, large enough to comfortably accomodate even the largest of your distant kin, and the diversity of clans here to meet you was equally fascinating.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum is to the east, the doors to the Great Hall are west, and if your wings are up for it, you could return to the skies and fly up (where Constance circles) or back down to the forest floor.&#x000A;&#x000A;A thick mist surrounds you, summoned by your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-51"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-51">
    <command xml:space="preserve">in</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Upper Great Hall&#x000A;The small platform just inside the huge double doors of the Great Hall overlooks the hall below, with plenty of space for people of all sizes and shapes to comfortably launch themselves from a smoothly-grown mahogany branch, wrapping around the whole platform.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Upper Great Hall&#x000A;The small platform just inside the huge double doors of the Great Hall overlooks the hall below, with plenty of space for people of all sizes and shapes to comfortably launch themselves from a smoothly-grown mahogany branch, wrapping around the whole platform.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-52"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-52">
    <command xml:space="preserve">d</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You spread your wings to their full extent before launching yourself downward.  You muscles protest, but even just being able to glide again is heavenly.&#x000A;&#x000A;Lower Great Hall&#x000A;The floor of the Great Hall is cleared of the myriad perches and decorations that are brought out for visiting delegations.  It breathes potential, bursting with what it could be, if only.  You wonder if there would even be enough staff to prepare it for a new delegation, with so many sick.  Not that delegations are common, nowadays.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the display nooks around the edges of the hall are all manner of artifacts from across many ages.&#x000A;&#x000A;In one of the nooks are two posts, designed for displaying ancient hunting cloaks.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You spread your wings to their full extent before launching yourself downward.  You muscles protest, but even just being able to glide again is heavenly.&#x000A;&#x000A;Lower Great Hall&#x000A;The floor of the Great Hall is cleared of the myriad perches and decorations that are brought out for visiting delegations.  It breathes potential, bursting with what it could be, if only.  You wonder if there would even be enough staff to prepare it for a new delegation, with so many sick.  Not that delegations are common, nowadays.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the display nooks around the edges of the hall are all manner of artifacts from across many ages.&#x000A;&#x000A;In one of the nooks are two posts, designed for displaying ancient hunting cloaks.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-53"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-53">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x nooks</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You could spend weeks in here if you were allowed, just cataloguing and recording your impressions of all the artifacts that fill the nooks surrounding the floor.  But right now, all you wanted to do was check to make sure the cloaks are still here.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
