    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-60">
    <command xml:space="preserve">1</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">[Ask her about scrolls.]&#x000A;&#x000A;"What do you do with scrolls?" you ask.&#x000A;&#x000A;Constance scoffs.  "Read them!" she exclaims, then laughs, as another thought occurs to her. "Which is the one thing you can't do with the scrolls in the capsae, because nobody knows..."  She trails off, and gives you another look.  "Wait, really?  You?"&#x000A;&#x000A;1) Tell her what you can do.&#x000A;2) OK, I'm a tester and I need to skip ahead and be Constance, fiddling with scrolls and stuff.&#x000A;3) I'm also a tester, and I just want to go back to the beginning of this conversation.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">[Ask her about scrolls.]&#x000A;&#x000A;"What do you do with scrolls?" you ask.&#x000A;&#x000A;Constance scoffs.  "Read them!" she exclaims, then laughs, as another thought occurs to her. "Which is the one thing you can't do with the scrolls in the capsae, because nobody knows..."  She trails off, and gives you another look.  "Wait, really?  You?"&#x000A;&#x000A;1) Tell her what you can do.&#x000A;2) OK, I'm a tester and I need to skip ahead and be Constance, fiddling with scrolls and stuff.&#x000A;3) I'm also a tester, and I just want to go back to the beginning of this conversation.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-61"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-61">
    <command xml:space="preserve">1</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">[Tell her what you can do.]&#x000A;&#x000A;"You've seen the scrolls themselves?  The writing on them?"&#x000A;&#x000A;"'Indeed,'" Constance replies, raising an eyebrow.  You grin.&#x000A;&#x000A;"What you may not know is that those symbols are not found in any other form of known writing.  There are fragments of writing from before the capsae.  They differ.  Some say it is the language of the gods themselves."&#x000A;&#x000A;"Woo, fancy," says Constance.  "In other words, they're gibberish."&#x000A;&#x000A;"No," you reply.  "I can read them."&#x000A;&#x000A;"Oh?  What do they say?" Constance asks.&#x000A;&#x000A;1) Tell her the truth.&#x000A;2) Wax poetical a bit.&#x000A;3) OK, I'm a tester and I need to skip ahead and be Constance, fiddling with scrolls and stuff.&#x000A;4) I'm also a tester, and I just want to go back to the beginning of this conversation.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">[Tell her what you can do.]&#x000A;&#x000A;"You've seen the scrolls themselves?  The writing on them?"&#x000A;&#x000A;"'Indeed,'" Constance replies, raising an eyebrow.  You grin.&#x000A;&#x000A;"What you may not know is that those symbols are not found in any other form of known writing.  There are fragments of writing from before the capsae.  They differ.  Some say it is the language of the gods themselves."&#x000A;&#x000A;"Woo, fancy," says Constance.  "In other words, they're gibberish."&#x000A;&#x000A;"No," you reply.  "I can read them."&#x000A;&#x000A;"Oh?  What do they say?" Constance asks.&#x000A;&#x000A;1) Tell her the truth.&#x000A;2) Wax poetical a bit.&#x000A;3) OK, I'm a tester and I need to skip ahead and be Constance, fiddling with scrolls and stuff.&#x000A;4) I'm also a tester, and I just want to go back to the beginning of this conversation.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-62"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-62">
    <command xml:space="preserve">1</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">[Tell her the truth.]&#x000A;&#x000A;"I don't know," you tell her.&#x000A;&#x000A;Constance sputters.  "But you--" she begins, then cuts herself off, looking at you askance again.  She's a clever woman.  You wait, tipping your wings synchronously with hers as you turn into another circuit.&#x000A;&#x000A;"So.  You learned the language from somewhere."  She thinks.  You wait.  "No, you said the symbols matched no other writing.  You were born knowing the language.  It's your heritage, as I was born knowing how to summon mist."&#x000A;&#x000A;You let her think, the lack of any contradiction from you enough of an encouragement.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Which means you've either just never seen an actual scroll--which seems unlikely; the queen didn't get mad at you until several days had passed--or," she slows down, but continues, "or you were born with the ability to read, but not understand."&#x000A;&#x000A;"Inde--"  Constance shoots you warning look.  "Yes.  That's it exactly.  Congratulations."  You bob your head and splay your wingfeathers in a grin of approval.&#x000A;&#x000A;"So, you want to read a capsa's scroll.  And you won't know what you're reading." says Constance.&#x000A;&#x000A;1) Share your speculation.&#x000A;2) OK, I'm a tester and I need to skip ahead and be Constance, fiddling with scrolls and stuff.&#x000A;3) I'm also a tester, and I just want to go back to the beginning of this conversation.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">[Tell her the truth.]&#x000A;&#x000A;"I don't know," you tell her.&#x000A;&#x000A;Constance sputters.  "But you--" she begins, then cuts herself off, looking at you askance again.  She's a clever woman.  You wait, tipping your wings synchronously with hers as you turn into another circuit.&#x000A;&#x000A;"So.  You learned the language from somewhere."  She thinks.  You wait.  "No, you said the symbols matched no other writing.  You were born knowing the language.  It's your heritage, as I was born knowing how to summon mist."&#x000A;&#x000A;You let her think, the lack of any contradiction from you enough of an encouragement.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Which means you've either just never seen an actual scroll--which seems unlikely; the queen didn't get mad at you until several days had passed--or," she slows down, but continues, "or you were born with the ability to read, but not understand."&#x000A;&#x000A;"Inde--"  Constance shoots you warning look.  "Yes.  That's it exactly.  Congratulations."  You bob your head and splay your wingfeathers in a grin of approval.&#x000A;&#x000A;"So, you want to read a capsa's scroll.  And you won't know what you're reading." says Constance.&#x000A;&#x000A;1) Share your speculation.&#x000A;2) OK, I'm a tester and I need to skip ahead and be Constance, fiddling with scrolls and stuff.&#x000A;3) I'm also a tester, and I just want to go back to the beginning of this conversation.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
