    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-72">
    <command xml:space="preserve">1</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">[Figure out what's next.]&#x000A;&#x000A;"So, what do we do next?" you ask.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I can sense the capsae.  Taclor, health, is in the Royal Quarters.  And with Igram, which you got from the Librum, I can lead you to it," Horatio tells you.  "We'll ned something from the Great Hall.  I'll meet you there."&#x000A;&#x000A;"What does it--you know, never mind, you obviously don't want to tell me," you say.  "Fine.  Let's go."  You turn to your new task.&#x000A;&#x000A;High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is here, watching you with quiet aplomb and patience.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;With a solemn nod to you, Horatio tells you to meet him in the Great Hall with the black capsa, then turns and glides away.&#x000A;&#x000A;Your wound aches.  You look down at it, and it's still open and bleeding.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">[Figure out what's next.]&#x000A;&#x000A;"So, what do we do next?" you ask.&#x000A;&#x000A;"I can sense the capsae.  Taclor, health, is in the Royal Quarters.  And with Igram, which you got from the Librum, I can lead you to it," Horatio tells you.  "We'll ned something from the Great Hall.  I'll meet you there."&#x000A;&#x000A;"What does it--you know, never mind, you obviously don't want to tell me," you say.  "Fine.  Let's go."  You turn to your new task.&#x000A;&#x000A;High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is here, watching you with quiet aplomb and patience.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;With a solemn nod to you, Horatio tells you to meet him in the Great Hall with the black capsa, then turns and glides away.&#x000A;&#x000A;Your wound aches.  You look down at it, and it's still open and bleeding.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-73"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-73">
    <command xml:space="preserve">close purple</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You close the purple capsa of opening.&#x000A;&#x000A;You feel your skin prickle where you were wounded, and look down.  To your amazement, your wound has closed and the bleeding stopped.  As you watch, even the line from the cut disappears, and the feathers around it fluff out again.&#x000A;&#x000A;It's the scroll of Health.  It has to be.  It's actually here!  And active.  Hmm.&#x000A;&#x000A;From everywhere in the Aerie, you hear the woodpeckers drumming in the Pounding dialect: "Reset Locks!  Repeat!  Reset Locks!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You close the purple capsa of opening.&#x000A;&#x000A;You feel your skin prickle where you were wounded, and look down.  To your amazement, your wound has closed and the bleeding stopped.  As you watch, even the line from the cut disappears, and the feathers around it fluff out again.&#x000A;&#x000A;It's the scroll of Health.  It has to be.  It's actually here!  And active.  Hmm.&#x000A;&#x000A;From everywhere in the Aerie, you hear the woodpeckers drumming in the Pounding dialect: "Reset Locks!  Repeat!  Reset Locks!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-74"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-74">
    <command xml:space="preserve">open purple</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You open the purple capsa of opening, revealing a scroll of rezrov.&#x000A;&#x000A;As you open the purple capsa, an almost-palpable wave of force emanates from it, as the power of the revealed scroll of rezrov is released.&#x000A;&#x000A;The magic of the blue capsa of mist prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the black capsa prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the gold capsa of down prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the red capsa of hasten prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You open the purple capsa of opening, revealing a scroll of rezrov.&#x000A;&#x000A;As you open the purple capsa, an almost-palpable wave of force emanates from it, as the power of the revealed scroll of rezrov is released.&#x000A;&#x000A;The magic of the blue capsa of mist prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the black capsa prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the gold capsa of down prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the red capsa of hasten prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-75"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-75">
    <command xml:space="preserve">d</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You tuck in your wings and dive down towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You tuck in your wings and dive down towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-76"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-76">
    <command xml:space="preserve">in</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Upper Great Hall&#x000A;There is a small platform just inside the huge double doors of the Great Hall, and that's it.  The platform is lined with a single elegant grown-mahogany branch that wraps around the whole platform.  It varies in size and thickness, so that all types of feet fit somewhere along it, so people can comfortably launch themselves into the air to glide down to the floor level, or grab it for stability as they return.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Upper Great Hall&#x000A;There is a small platform just inside the huge double doors of the Great Hall, and that's it.  The platform is lined with a single elegant grown-mahogany branch that wraps around the whole platform.  It varies in size and thickness, so that all types of feet fit somewhere along it, so people can comfortably launch themselves into the air to glide down to the floor level, or grab it for stability as they return.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-77"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-77">
    <command xml:space="preserve">d</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You step on to your favorite spot on the mahogany branch, and launch yourself downward in a graceful glide.&#x000A;&#x000A;Lower Great Hall&#x000A;When not prepared for a particular occasion, like now, the floor of the Great Hall is cleared of everything extraneous.  The exposed floor is absolutely exquisite, with swooping lines interspersed with starbursts, all in multicolored woods of all hues.  What doesn't change about the Great Hall floor is the display nooks along the sides: at least twenty nooks containing all manner of artifacts from around the world.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is here, watching you with quiet aplomb and patience.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You step on to your favorite spot on the mahogany branch, and launch yourself downward in a graceful glide.&#x000A;&#x000A;Lower Great Hall&#x000A;When not prepared for a particular occasion, like now, the floor of the Great Hall is cleared of everything extraneous.  The exposed floor is absolutely exquisite, with swooping lines interspersed with starbursts, all in multicolored woods of all hues.  What doesn't change about the Great Hall floor is the display nooks along the sides: at least twenty nooks containing all manner of artifacts from around the world.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is here, watching you with quiet aplomb and patience.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-78"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-78">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x horatio</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Horatio is an ancient Buzzard Clan sage of sorts, you suppose, given that he was jailed for heresy back in the day.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Horatio is an ancient Buzzard Clan sage of sorts, you suppose, given that he was jailed for heresy back in the day.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-79"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-79">
    <command xml:space="preserve">open gold</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You open the gold capsa of down, revealing a scroll of rudenj.&#x000A;&#x000A;Immediately, dozens of artifacts and collectibles rain down, flying out of the display nooks all around you.  When the Raven Guard shows up, it's almost more of a rescue than a capture, as they have to dig you out of a huge pile of detritus before finally being able to reach and close the gold capsa.&#x000A;&#x000A;It's still definitely also a capture, though.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;    *** You have, indeed, been captured. ***&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;Would you like to RESTART, RESTORE a saved game, QUIT, or UNDO the last command?&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You open the gold capsa of down, revealing a scroll of rudenj.&#x000A;&#x000A;Immediately, dozens of artifacts and collectibles rain down, flying out of the display nooks all around you.  When the Raven Guard shows up, it's almost more of a rescue than a capture, as they have to dig you out of a huge pile of detritus before finally being able to reach and close the gold capsa.&#x000A;&#x000A;It's still definitely also a capture, though.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;    *** You have, indeed, been captured. ***&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;Would you like to RESTART, RESTORE a saved game, QUIT, or UNDO the last command?&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-80"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-80">
    <command xml:space="preserve">undo</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Lower Great Hall&#x000A;[Previous turn undone.]&#x000A;&#x000A;When not prepared for a particular occasion, like now, the floor of the Great Hall is cleared of everything extraneous.  The exposed floor is absolutely exquisite, with swooping lines interspersed with starbursts, all in multicolored woods of all hues.  What doesn't change about the Great Hall floor is the display nooks along the sides: at least twenty nooks containing all manner of artifacts from around the world.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
