  <item nodeId="node-98">
    <command xml:space="preserve">test map</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(Testing.)&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[1] d&#x000A;You tuck in your wings and dive down towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[2] u&#x000A;&#x000A;High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[3] n&#x000A;You tuck in your wings and dive down north towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Royal Gardens&#x000A;The Royal Gardens is the most lavishly opulent and sensuous entrance to any aerie you've seen in your life.  Trees, vines, and flowers of every variety spring up from everywhere, each seemingly placed in the exactly appropriate spot.  The landing cradle next to the garden door to the Royal Quarters themselves is nestled between gracious arcs of poplar trunks, each bedecked with shaded and inviting roosts.  Which, as you know from your childhood days swooping and laughing through these gardens, invariably contain at least eight guards.  Probably ten or more today.&#x000A;&#x000A;From here, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.  The Great Hall is to the south, and the Librum to the southeast.  The door to the very-guarded Royal Quarters is to the north.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[4] u&#x000A;&#x000A;High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[5] e&#x000A;You tuck in your wings and dive down east towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A lone Raven guard stands in front of the door, dark eyes shifting as she watches the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[6] u&#x000A;&#x000A;High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[7] d&#x000A;You tuck in your wings and dive down towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[8] e&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A lone Raven guard stands in front of the door, dark eyes shifting as she watches the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[9] nw&#x000A;&#x000A;Royal Gardens&#x000A;The Royal Gardens is the most lavishly opulent and sensuous entrance to any aerie you've seen in your life.  Trees, vines, and flowers of every variety spring up from everywhere, each seemingly placed in the exactly appropriate spot.  The landing cradle next to the garden door to the Royal Quarters themselves is nestled between gracious arcs of poplar trunks, each bedecked with shaded and inviting roosts.  Which, as you know from your childhood days swooping and laughing through these gardens, invariably contain at least eight guards.  Probably ten or more today.&#x000A;&#x000A;From here, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.  The Great Hall is to the south, and the Librum to the southeast.  The door to the very-guarded Royal Quarters is to the north.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[10] s&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[11] n&#x000A;&#x000A;Royal Gardens&#x000A;The Royal Gardens is the most lavishly opulent and sensuous entrance to any aerie you've seen in your life.  Trees, vines, and flowers of every variety spring up from everywhere, each seemingly placed in the exactly appropriate spot.  The landing cradle next to the garden door to the Royal Quarters themselves is nestled between gracious arcs of poplar trunks, each bedecked with shaded and inviting roosts.  Which, as you know from your childhood days swooping and laughing through these gardens, invariably contain at least eight guards.  Probably ten or more today.&#x000A;&#x000A;From here, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.  The Great Hall is to the south, and the Librum to the southeast.  The door to the very-guarded Royal Quarters is to the north.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[12] se&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A lone Raven guard stands in front of the door, dark eyes shifting as she watches the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[13] w&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[14] d&#x000A;You tuck in your wings and dive down into the forest below the Aerie, dodging tightly-spaced trees with acrobatic precision.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the Forest&#x000A;The trees below the Royal Aerie grow more closely together than in the rest of the forest, and include a wider variety, so that differently-colored woods could be incorporated into the buildings above.  This makes it harder to navigate down here--or it would if you weren't so amazing at navigation.&#x000A;&#x000A;Even through the mist, your sharp eyes spot a fine net, stretched between the trees.  It seems to be set to prevent anyone from coming up from the forest below.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[15] u&#x000A;You gracefully flit between the trees back up above the canopy.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[16] e&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A lone Raven guard stands in front of the door, dark eyes shifting as she watches the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[17] d&#x000A;You tuck in your wings and dive down into the forest below the Aerie, dodging tightly-spaced trees with acrobatic precision.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the Forest&#x000A;The trees below the Royal Aerie grow more closely together than in the rest of the forest, and include a wider variety, so that differently-colored woods could be incorporated into the buildings above.  This makes it harder to navigate down here--or it would if you weren't so amazing at navigation.&#x000A;&#x000A;Even through the mist, your sharp eyes spot a fine net, stretched between the trees.  It seems to be set to prevent anyone from coming up from the forest below.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[18] e&#x000A;You gracefully flit between the trees back up east above the canopy.&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A lone Raven guard stands in front of the door, dark eyes shifting as she watches the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[19] d&#x000A;You tuck in your wings and dive down into the forest below the Aerie, dodging tightly-spaced trees with acrobatic precision.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the Forest&#x000A;The trees below the Royal Aerie grow more closely together than in the rest of the forest, and include a wider variety, so that differently-colored woods could be incorporated into the buildings above.  This makes it harder to navigate down here--or it would if you weren't so amazing at navigation.&#x000A;&#x000A;Even through the mist, your sharp eyes spot a fine net, stretched between the trees.  It seems to be set to prevent anyone from coming up from the forest below.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[20] n&#x000A;You gracefully flit between the trees back up north above the canopy.&#x000A;&#x000A;Royal Gardens&#x000A;The Royal Gardens is the most lavishly opulent and sensuous entrance to any aerie you've seen in your life.  Trees, vines, and flowers of every variety spring up from everywhere, each seemingly placed in the exactly appropriate spot.  The landing cradle next to the garden door to the Royal Quarters themselves is nestled between gracious arcs of poplar trunks, each bedecked with shaded and inviting roosts.  Which, as you know from your childhood days swooping and laughing through these gardens, invariably contain at least eight guards.  Probably ten or more today.&#x000A;&#x000A;From here, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.  The Great Hall is to the south, and the Librum to the southeast.  The door to the very-guarded Royal Quarters is to the north.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[21] d&#x000A;You tuck in your wings and dive down into the forest below the Aerie, dodging tightly-spaced trees with acrobatic precision.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the Forest&#x000A;The trees below the Royal Aerie grow more closely together than in the rest of the forest, and include a wider variety, so that differently-colored woods could be incorporated into the buildings above.  This makes it harder to navigate down here--or it would if you weren't so amazing at navigation.&#x000A;&#x000A;Even through the mist, your sharp eyes spot a fine net, stretched between the trees.  It seems to be set to prevent anyone from coming up from the forest below.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[22] u&#x000A;You gracefully flit between the trees back up above the canopy.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[23] u&#x000A;&#x000A;High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">(Testing.)&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[1] d&#x000A;You tuck in your wings and dive down towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[2] u&#x000A;&#x000A;High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[3] n&#x000A;You tuck in your wings and dive down north towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Royal Gardens&#x000A;The Royal Gardens is the most lavishly opulent and sensuous entrance to any aerie you've seen in your life.  Trees, vines, and flowers of every variety spring up from everywhere, each seemingly placed in the exactly appropriate spot.  The landing cradle next to the garden door to the Royal Quarters themselves is nestled between gracious arcs of poplar trunks, each bedecked with shaded and inviting roosts.  Which, as you know from your childhood days swooping and laughing through these gardens, invariably contain at least eight guards.  Probably ten or more today.&#x000A;&#x000A;From here, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.  The Great Hall is to the south, and the Librum to the southeast.  The door to the very-guarded Royal Quarters is to the north.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[4] u&#x000A;&#x000A;High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[5] e&#x000A;You tuck in your wings and dive down east towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A lone Raven guard stands in front of the door, dark eyes shifting as she watches the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[6] u&#x000A;&#x000A;High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[7] d&#x000A;You tuck in your wings and dive down towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[8] e&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A lone Raven guard stands in front of the door, dark eyes shifting as she watches the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[9] nw&#x000A;&#x000A;Royal Gardens&#x000A;The Royal Gardens is the most lavishly opulent and sensuous entrance to any aerie you've seen in your life.  