  <item nodeId="node-101">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You wait, expectantly.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You wait, expectantly.</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-102"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-102">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Silently, your cell door unlocks, then swings open.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Silently, your cell door unlocks, then swings open.</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-103"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-103">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Well above your cell, you sense quiste, rezrov, and rudenj settle in their movements until they make lazy circles, high above the Aerie. Igram and taclor remain in place, quiet.&#x000A;&#x000A;It is time.&#x000A;&#x000A;Forgotten Brig&#x000A;A small but cosy cell, grown with austerity but basic comfort in mind.  Your now-open cell door leads west.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Well above your cell, you sense quiste, rezrov, and rudenj settle in their movements until they make lazy circles, high above the Aerie. Igram and taclor remain in place, quiet.&#x000A;&#x000A;It is time.&#x000A;&#x000A;Forgotten Brig&#x000A;A small but cosy cell, grown with austerity but basic comfort in mind.  Your now-open cell door leads west.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-104"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-104">
    <command xml:space="preserve">test quick_horatio</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(Testing.)&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[1] x cell&#x000A;(cell contents)&#x000A;A straight roost by a desk for writing, and a scooped roost for sleeping.  Enough space to spread your wings.  A rope wall for excercise.  Not bad.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[2] x desk&#x000A;A straight roost by a desk for writing, and a scooped roost for sleeping.  Enough space to spread your wings.  A rope wall for excercise.  Not bad.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[3] x cell door&#x000A;Ironwood-grown and maintained; your cell door is open.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[4] w&#x000A;&#x000A;Disused Hallway&#x000A;The only time you ever saw anyone in this hallway was when Georg came to give you your meals, or clean the cell.  The living walls, still elegantly patterned, even here, self-replenish, and the floor carries away shed bark through the grate.  It leads west into the living area, and your old cell door leads east.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[5] w&#x000A;Your place is not with the denizens of this Aerie, but with the prodigal daughter, now returned, and the capsa she seeks.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[6] close grate&#x000A;You close the grate.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[7] open grate&#x000A;You grasp the grate with your talons and carefully fold it upward, allowing access.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[8] enter grate&#x000A;You flatten yourself to the floor and, hearing your bones creak, roll into the space behind the grate.  Using your minimal throck ability, you whisper a song to the veins of this place: "I am extra.  I am not needed.  Take me from this place, which will renew itself through my absence."&#x000A;&#x000A;After a few moments, you feel an undulation in the slick rippled floor beneath you, and you are compressed even further, as its peristalsis slides you slowly, and then more rapidly, away from your only home for the last ten years.  Then with a sudden &gt;plop&lt;, you're ejected into space.&#x000A;&#x000A;You try to spread your wings, but your reaction time is not what it was, and you hit wirey netting before fully stopping yourself.&#x000A;&#x000A;No matter.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the Forest&#x000A;The tightly-growing trees and thick fog surround you tightly.  It would be oppressive, but for the echo of the Throckwright song you can just sense, flowing through the veins of these trees still.  That, and the fact that you've been confined to a single room for a decade, so any contrast is welcome.&#x000A;&#x000A;The net that caught you stretches in every direction, preventing both entrance to and egress from the rest of the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;A thick mist surrounds you, summoned by your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[9] u&#x000A;Forcing your tired wings to flap again, you rise above the forest floor, past the level of your cell, up above the canopy.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall was the first you ever saw of this Aerie, when you arrived ten years ago in the entourage of the Waterfowl delegation.  You were impressed by the huge double doors of the Great Hall, large enough to comfortably accomodate even the largest of your distant kin, and the diversity of clans here to meet you was equally fascinating.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum is to the east, the doors to the Great Hall are west, and if your wings are up for it, you could return to the skies and fly up (where Constance circles) or back down to the forest floor.&#x000A;&#x000A;A thick mist surrounds you, summoned by your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[10] u&#x000A;&#x000A;High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;There's nothing to see here, this high above the Aerie; just a thick mist in every direction.  You would have never been able to find Constance if she hadn't been carrying a capsa or two.  You trust that if you circle down from here, you'll be able to find your way once you reach some landmarks.&#x000A;&#x000A;Constance, a powerful Falcon Clan female, is here, her large black eyes watching you with fierce intensity.&#x000A;&#x000A;A thick mist surrounds you, summoned by your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;                                                              *    *    *</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">(Testing.)&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[1] x cell&#x000A;(cell contents)&#x000A;A straight roost by a desk for writing, and a scooped roost for sleeping.  Enough space to spread your wings.  A rope wall for excercise.  Not bad.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[2] x desk&#x000A;A straight roost by a desk for writing, and a scooped roost for sleeping.  Enough space to spread your wings.  A rope wall for excercise.  Not bad.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[3] x cell door&#x000A;Ironwood-grown and maintained; your cell door is open.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[4] w&#x000A;&#x000A;Disused Hallway&#x000A;The only time you ever saw anyone in this hallway was when Georg came to give you your meals, or clean the cell.  The living walls, still elegantly patterned, even here, self-replenish, and the floor carries away shed bark through the grate.  It leads west into the living area, and your old cell door leads east.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[5] w&#x000A;Your place is not with the denizens of this Aerie, but with the prodigal daughter, now returned, and the capsa she seeks.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[6] close grate&#x000A;You close the grate.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[7] open grate&#x000A;You grasp the grate with your talons and carefully fold it upward, allowing access.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[8] enter grate&#x000A;You flatten yourself to the floor and, hearing your bones creak, roll into the space behind the grate.  Using your minimal throck ability, you whisper a song to the veins of this place: "I am extra.  I am not needed.  Take me from this place, which will renew itself through my absence."&#x000A;&#x000A;After a few moments, you feel an undulation in the slick rippled floor beneath you, and you are compressed even further, as its peristalsis slides you slowly, and then more rapidly, away from your only home for the last ten years.  Then with a sudden &gt;plop&lt;, you're ejected into space.&#x000A;&#x000A;You try to spread your wings, but your reaction time is not what it was, and you hit wirey netting before fully stopping yourself.&#x000A;&#x000A;No matter.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the Forest&#x000A;The tightly-growing trees and thick fog surround you tightly.  It would be oppressive, but for the echo of the Throckwright song you can just sense, flowing through the veins of these trees still.  That, and the fact that you've been confined to a single room for a decade, so any contrast is welcome.&#x000A;&#x000A;The net that caught you stretches in every direction, preventing both entrance to and egress from the rest of the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;A thick mist surrounds you, summoned by your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[9] u&#x000A;Forcing your tired wings to flap again, you rise above the forest floor, past the level of your cell, up above the canopy.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall was the first you ever saw of this Aerie, when you arrived ten years ago in the entourage of the Waterfowl delegation.  You were impressed by the huge double doors of the Great Hall, large enough to comfortably accomodate even the largest of your distant kin, and the diversity of clans here to meet you was equally fascinating.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum is to the east, the doors to the Great Hall are west, and if your wings are up for it, you could return to the skies and fly up (where Constance circles) or back down to the forest floor.&#x000A;&#x000A;A thick mist surrounds you, summoned by your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[10] u&#x000A;&#x000A;High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;There's nothing to see here, this high above the Aerie; just a thick mist in every direction.  You would have never been able to find Constance if she hadn't been carrying a capsa or two.  You trust that if you circle down from here, you'll be able to find your way once you reach some landmarks.&#x000A;&#x000A;Constance, a powerful Falcon Clan female, is here, her large black eyes watching you with fierce intensity.&#x000A;&#x000A;A thick mist surrounds you, summoned by your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;                                                              *    *    *</commentary>
