  <item nodeId="node-165">
    <command xml:space="preserve">w</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Raven Guard pursues you determinedly through the thin mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Raven Guard pursues you determinedly through the thin mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-166"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-166">
    <command xml:space="preserve">w</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(first opening the huge double doors of the Great Hall)&#x000A;The Raven Guard is not going to stop chasing you to give you enough time to open the huge double doors of the Great Hall.  Though perhaps if you explained that you only wanted to go into an enclosed space so they could better surround and capture you, they'd consider it?&#x000A;&#x000A;The guards charge, but you manage to evade their uncoordinated attack.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">(first opening the huge double doors of the Great Hall)&#x000A;The Raven Guard is not going to stop chasing you to give you enough time to open the huge double doors of the Great Hall.  Though perhaps if you explained that you only wanted to go into an enclosed space so they could better surround and capture you, they'd consider it?&#x000A;&#x000A;The guards charge, but you manage to evade their uncoordinated attack.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-167"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-167">
    <command xml:space="preserve">undo</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;[Previous turn undone.]&#x000A;&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;[Previous turn undone.]&#x000A;&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
