  <item nodeId="node-175">
    <command xml:space="preserve">open purple</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You open the purple capsa of opening, revealing a scroll of rezrov.&#x000A;&#x000A;As you open the purple capsa, an almost-palpable wave of force emanates from it, as the power of the revealed scroll of rezrov is released.&#x000A;&#x000A;The magic of the blue capsa of mist prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the gold capsa of down prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the red capsa of hasten prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;&#x000A;From... well, from everywhere in the Aerie, it seems, Woodpeckers start drumming out messages in their Pounding dialect:  "Intruder! Estimated direction is..." and then each one individually seems to be telegraphing the direction from them to you.  You can't discern any one drummer from any other drummer, but you can at least tell that each seems to be drumming on sheets of metal that differ from each other, so every frequency is unique.  That makes the information somewhat useless to you, because you've not been trained to distinguish Pounding at different frequencies.  And because you already know where you are.  Sadly, the Raven Guards are indeed trained to distinguish Pounding frequencies.&#x000A;&#x000A;And if they didn't know where you were, they do now.&#x000A;&#x000A;You suddenly feel warmer, and hear an exultant song of the sun in the distance.  The queen's Ikniq warriors are at it again, trained to try to burn away your fog.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You open the purple capsa of opening, revealing a scroll of rezrov.&#x000A;&#x000A;As you open the purple capsa, an almost-palpable wave of force emanates from it, as the power of the revealed scroll of rezrov is released.&#x000A;&#x000A;The magic of the blue capsa of mist prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the gold capsa of down prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the red capsa of hasten prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;&#x000A;From... well, from everywhere in the Aerie, it seems, Woodpeckers start drumming out messages in their Pounding dialect:  "Intruder! Estimated direction is..." and then each one individually seems to be telegraphing the direction from them to you.  You can't discern any one drummer from any other drummer, but you can at least tell that each seems to be drumming on sheets of metal that differ from each other, so every frequency is unique.  That makes the information somewhat useless to you, because you've not been trained to distinguish Pounding at different frequencies.  And because you already know where you are.  Sadly, the Raven Guards are indeed trained to distinguish Pounding frequencies.&#x000A;&#x000A;And if they didn't know where you were, they do now.&#x000A;&#x000A;You suddenly feel warmer, and hear an exultant song of the sun in the distance.  The queen's Ikniq warriors are at it again, trained to try to burn away your fog.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-176"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-176">
    <command xml:space="preserve">d</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You tuck in your wings and dive down towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;You've dived straight into a squad of Raven Guards, on their way up to accost you.  Fortunately, your speed helped you avoid most of them, but one guard's talon catches you on your side as you twist by them.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You tuck in your wings and dive down towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;You've dived straight into a squad of Raven Guards, on their way up to accost you.  Fortunately, your speed helped you avoid most of them, but one guard's talon catches you on your side as you twist by them.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-177"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-177">
    <command xml:space="preserve">d</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In the Forest&#x000A;The trees below the Royal Aerie grow more closely together than in the rest of the forest, and include a wider variety, so that differently-colored woods could be incorporated into the buildings above.  This makes it harder to navigate down here--or it would if you weren't so amazing at navigation.&#x000A;&#x000A;Even through the mist, your sharp eyes spot a fine net, stretched between the trees.  It seems to be set to prevent anyone from coming up from the forest below.&#x000A;&#x000A;You expertly twist at breakneck speeds, weaving through three Ash trunks, over a branch, and around and behind a Redwood, where you halt, twist, and dive straight down the trunk, out of view of any stray Raven.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Raven's frustrated caws echo in the thin mist.  In time, the woodpeckers cease their drumming, and the cawing fades as well.  Protocol would dictate that they return to guarding priority items.  If there were any reserves left, they would be called up, but the Red Plague has affected the Raven Guard as sorely as your own community.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">In the Forest&#x000A;The trees below the Royal Aerie grow more closely together than in the rest of the forest, and include a wider variety, so that differently-colored woods could be incorporated into the buildings above.  This makes it harder to navigate down here--or it would if you weren't so amazing at navigation.&#x000A;&#x000A;Even through the mist, your sharp eyes spot a fine net, stretched between the trees.  It seems to be set to prevent anyone from coming up from the forest below.&#x000A;&#x000A;You expertly twist at breakneck speeds, weaving through three Ash trunks, over a branch, and around and behind a Redwood, where you halt, twist, and dive straight down the trunk, out of view of any stray Raven.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Raven's frustrated caws echo in the thin mist.  In time, the woodpeckers cease their drumming, and the cawing fades as well.  Protocol would dictate that they return to guarding priority items.  If there were any reserves left, they would be called up, but the Red Plague has affected the Raven Guard as sorely as your own community.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-178"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-178">
    <command xml:space="preserve">e</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You gracefully flit between the trees back up east above the canopy.&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A lone Raven guard stands in front of the door, dark eyes shifting as she watches the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the cradle next to the guard is a small collection of tiny padlocks, each open.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is talking slowly to the lone guard about regrettable fashion choices from the youth of today, driving the guard quietly insane.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You gracefully flit between the trees back up east above the canopy.&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A lone Raven guard stands in front of the door, dark eyes shifting as she watches the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the cradle next to the guard is a small collection of tiny padlocks, each open.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is talking slowly to the lone guard about regrettable fashion choices from the youth of today, driving the guard quietly insane.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-179"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-179">
    <command xml:space="preserve">u</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-180"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-180">
    <command xml:space="preserve">e</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You tuck in your wings and dive down east towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A lone Raven guard stands in front of the door, dark eyes shifting as she watches the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the cradle next to the guard is a small collection of tiny padlocks, each open.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is talking slowly to the lone guard about whether the dot on the back of looks infected, driving the guard quietly insane.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You tuck in your wings and dive down east towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A lone Raven guard stands in front of the door, dark eyes shifting as she watches the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the cradle next to the guard is a small collection of tiny padlocks, each open.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is talking slowly to the lone guard about whether the dot on the back of looks infected, driving the guard quietly insane.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-181"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-181">
    <command xml:space="preserve">in</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Using the extra speed from your dive, you quietly plunge through the Librum door behind the distracted guard, pulling up sharply on the other side before crashing into anything.&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum&#x000A;The Librum contains two levels of scrolls and books, with easy access to all of the curving shelves, and plenty of reading roosts with natural and artificial lighting.  You know from your childhood where the best roosts are, and what sections contain the most exciting stories.  In the center of the lower room is a lavish display case, now hastily boarded over, which three days ago held the purple, gold, and red capsae.  The Librum Door is back up at the top level.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the back of the lower level, the storage cupboard Horatio told you about has fallen over, but the black capsa is in it, just as he said it would be.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Using the extra speed from your dive, you quietly plunge through the Librum door behind the distracted guard, pulling up sharply on the other side before crashing into anything.&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum&#x000A;The Librum contains two levels of scrolls and books, with easy access to all of the curving shelves, and plenty of reading roosts with natural and artificial lighting.  You know from your childhood where the best roosts are, and what sections contain the most exciting stories.  In the center of the lower room is a lavish display case, now hastily boarded over, which three days ago held the purple, gold, and red capsae.  The Librum Door is back up at the top level.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the back of the lower level, the storage cupboard Horatio told you about has fallen over, but the black capsa is in it, just as he said it would be.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-182"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-182">
    <command xml:space="preserve">open gold</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In case of emergencies, most things in the Librum were locked down so as to not fall over if the gold capsa of "down" was accidentally opened (though the old storage cabinet's attachments seem to not have held).  So nothing flies off the shelves to hit you when you open the gold capsa of "down" in here on purpose.  Which is good!  Less good is that since "down" now points straight at you, the guard outside was alerted to your presence.  She shows up at the door with a wicked grin.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;    *** You have been captured. ***&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;Would you like to RESTART, RESTORE a saved game, QUIT, or UNDO the last command?&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">In case of emergencies, most things in the Librum were locked down so as to not fall over if the gold capsa of "down" was accidentally opened (though the old storage cabinet's attachments seem to not have held).  So nothing flies off the shelves to hit you when you open the gold capsa of "down" in here on purpose.  Which is good!  Less good is that since "down" now points straight at you, the guard outside was alerted to your presence.  She shows up at the door with a wicked grin.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;    *** You have been captured. ***&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;Would you like to RESTART, RESTORE a saved game, QUIT, or UNDO the last command?&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-183"/>
    </children>
  </item>
