    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-233"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-233">
    <command xml:space="preserve">out</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Listening to Horatio talk with the guard, you enter the shadows just inside the Librum door, where you can watch the guard but not be seen.  When the moment is right, you launch yourself through, and back up into the safety of the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A lone Raven guard stands in front of the door, dark eyes shifting as she watches the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is talking quickly to the lone guard about his grandchildren, driving the guard quietly insane.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the cradle next to the guard is a small collection of tiny padlocks, each open.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Listening to Horatio talk with the guard, you enter the shadows just inside the Librum door, where you can watch the guard but not be seen.  When the moment is right, you launch yourself through, and back up into the safety of the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;Librum Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Librum is beautifully set with interlocking redwood and pine, suggesting shelves of books.  The Librum Door leads inward to the Librum itself.&#x000A;&#x000A;To the west is the Great Hall, and to the northwest is the Royal Quarters and Gardens.  You can also re-ascend to the skies or descend to the forest below.  The door to the Librum is to the east.&#x000A;&#x000A;A lone Raven guard stands in front of the door, dark eyes shifting as she watches the mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is talking quickly to the lone guard about his grandchildren, driving the guard quietly insane.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the cradle next to the guard is a small collection of tiny padlocks, each open.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-234"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-234">
    <command xml:space="preserve">w</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio glides out of the mist and circles near you.  He nods at the black capsa.  "Excellent work.  Now, we need something from the Great Hall."&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio glides through the open double doors of the Great Hall.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio glides out of the mist and circles near you.  He nods at the black capsa.  "Excellent work.  Now, we need something from the Great Hall."&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio glides through the open double doors of the Great Hall.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-235"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-235">
    <command xml:space="preserve">in</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Upper Great Hall&#x000A;There is a small platform just inside the huge double doors of the Great Hall, and that's it.  The platform is lined with a single elegant grown-mahogany branch that wraps around the whole platform.  It varies in size and thickness, so that all types of feet fit somewhere along it, so people can comfortably launch themselves into the air to glide down to the floor level, or grab it for stability as they return.&#x000A;&#x000A;The wooden bar that once held the Great Hall doors shut lies here, discarded.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Upper Great Hall&#x000A;There is a small platform just inside the huge double doors of the Great Hall, and that's it.  The platform is lined with a single elegant grown-mahogany branch that wraps around the whole platform.  It varies in size and thickness, so that all types of feet fit somewhere along it, so people can comfortably launch themselves into the air to glide down to the floor level, or grab it for stability as they return.&#x000A;&#x000A;The wooden bar that once held the Great Hall doors shut lies here, discarded.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-236"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-236">
    <command xml:space="preserve">d</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You step on to your favorite spot on the mahogany branch, and launch yourself downward in a graceful glide.&#x000A;&#x000A;Lower Great Hall&#x000A;When not prepared for a particular occasion, like now, the floor of the Great Hall is cleared of everything extraneous.  The exposed floor is absolutely exquisite, with swooping lines interspersed with starbursts, all in multicolored woods of all hues.  What doesn't change about the Great Hall floor is the display nooks along the sides: at least twenty nooks containing all manner of artifacts from around the world.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is here, watching you with quiet aplomb and patience.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle down and land near Horatio.  "So.  Now will you tell me what igram does and why it's so important?" you ask.&#x000A;&#x000A;"It is better to show you," he replies.  "Try it."&#x000A;&#x000A;You sigh.  Fine.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You step on to your favorite spot on the mahogany branch, and launch yourself downward in a graceful glide.&#x000A;&#x000A;Lower Great Hall&#x000A;When not prepared for a particular occasion, like now, the floor of the Great Hall is cleared of everything extraneous.  The exposed floor is absolutely exquisite, with swooping lines interspersed with starbursts, all in multicolored woods of all hues.  What doesn't change about the Great Hall floor is the display nooks along the sides: at least twenty nooks containing all manner of artifacts from around the world.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is here, watching you with quiet aplomb and patience.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle down and land near Horatio.  "So.  Now will you tell me what igram does and why it's so important?" you ask.&#x000A;&#x000A;"It is better to show you," he replies.  "Try it."&#x000A;&#x000A;You sigh.  Fine.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-237"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-237">
    <command xml:space="preserve">open black</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(the black capsa)&#x000A;You open the black capsa, revealing a scroll of igram.&#x000A;&#x000A;For a moment, the purple capsa seems to flicker.  But you look again, and nothing seems to have changed.&#x000A;Suddenly, two hunting cloaks in a display of ancient pre-historical artifacts disappear!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">(the black capsa)&#x000A;You open the black capsa, revealing a scroll of igram.&#x000A;&#x000A;For a moment, the purple capsa seems to flicker.  But you look again, and nothing seems to have changed.&#x000A;Suddenly, two hunting cloaks in a display of ancient pre-historical artifacts disappear!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-238"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-238">
    <command xml:space="preserve">l</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Lower Great Hall&#x000A;When not prepared for a particular occasion, like now, the floor of the Great Hall is cleared of everything extraneous.  The exposed floor is absolutely exquisite, with swooping lines interspersed with starbursts, all in multicolored woods of all hues.  What doesn't change about the Great Hall floor is the display nooks along the sides: at least twenty nooks containing all manner of artifacts from around the world.&#x000A;&#x000A;In one of the nooks are two posts, designed for displaying ancient hunting cloaks.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is here, watching you with quiet aplomb and patience.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Lower Great Hall&#x000A;When not prepared for a particular occasion, like now, the floor of the Great Hall is cleared of everything extraneous.  The exposed floor is absolutely exquisite, with swooping lines interspersed with starbursts, all in multicolored woods of all hues.  What doesn't change about the Great Hall floor is the display nooks along the sides: at least twenty nooks containing all manner of artifacts from around the world.&#x000A;&#x000A;In one of the nooks are two posts, designed for displaying ancient hunting cloaks.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio is here, watching you with quiet aplomb and patience.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-239"/>
    </children>
  </item>
