  <item nodeId="node-250">
    <command xml:space="preserve">close it</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You close the purple capsa of opening.&#x000A;&#x000A;You feel your skin prickle where you were wounded, and look down.  To your amazement, your wound has closed and the bleeding stopped.  As you watch, even the line from the cut disappears, and the feathers around it fluff out again.&#x000A;&#x000A;It's the scroll of Health.  It has to be.  It's actually here!  And active.  Hmm.&#x000A;&#x000A;From everywhere in the Aerie, you hear the woodpeckers drumming in the Pounding dialect: "Reset Locks!  Repeat!  Reset Locks!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You close the purple capsa of opening.&#x000A;&#x000A;You feel your skin prickle where you were wounded, and look down.  To your amazement, your wound has closed and the bleeding stopped.  As you watch, even the line from the cut disappears, and the feathers around it fluff out again.&#x000A;&#x000A;It's the scroll of Health.  It has to be.  It's actually here!  And active.  Hmm.&#x000A;&#x000A;From everywhere in the Aerie, you hear the woodpeckers drumming in the Pounding dialect: "Reset Locks!  Repeat!  Reset Locks!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-251"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-251">
    <command xml:space="preserve">open it</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You open the purple capsa of opening, revealing a scroll of rezrov.&#x000A;&#x000A;As you open the purple capsa, an almost-palpable wave of force emanates from it, as the power of the revealed scroll of rezrov is released.&#x000A;&#x000A;The magic of the blue capsa of mist prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the black capsa prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the gold capsa of down prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You open the purple capsa of opening, revealing a scroll of rezrov.&#x000A;&#x000A;As you open the purple capsa, an almost-palpable wave of force emanates from it, as the power of the revealed scroll of rezrov is released.&#x000A;&#x000A;The magic of the blue capsa of mist prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the black capsa prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the gold capsa of down prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-252"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-252">
    <command xml:space="preserve">out</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-253"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-253">
    <command xml:space="preserve">n</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Royal Gardens&#x000A;The Royal Gardens is the most lavishly opulent and sensuous entrance to any aerie you've seen in your life.  Trees, vines, and flowers of every variety spring up from everywhere, each seemingly placed in the exactly appropriate spot.  The landing cradle next to the garden door to the Royal Quarters themselves is nestled between gracious arcs of poplar trunks, each bedecked with shaded and inviting roosts.  Which, as you know from your childhood days swooping and laughing through these gardens, invariably contain at least eight guards.  Probably ten or more today.&#x000A;&#x000A;From here, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.  The Great Hall is to the south, and the Librum to the southeast.  The door to the very-guarded Royal Quarters is to the north.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">Royal Gardens&#x000A;The Royal Gardens is the most lavishly opulent and sensuous entrance to any aerie you've seen in your life.  Trees, vines, and flowers of every variety spring up from everywhere, each seemingly placed in the exactly appropriate spot.  The landing cradle next to the garden door to the Royal Quarters themselves is nestled between gracious arcs of poplar trunks, each bedecked with shaded and inviting roosts.  Which, as you know from your childhood days swooping and laughing through these gardens, invariably contain at least eight guards.  Probably ten or more today.&#x000A;&#x000A;From here, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.  The Great Hall is to the south, and the Librum to the southeast.  The door to the very-guarded Royal Quarters is to the north.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-254"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-254">
    <command xml:space="preserve">in</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">No way.  It wouldn't matter how fast you were or how thick the mist was.  You just can't get in there as you are without someone seeing you.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">No way.  It wouldn't matter how fast you were or how thick the mist was.  You just can't get in there as you are without someone seeing you.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
