    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-266">
    <command xml:space="preserve">i</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You are carrying:&#x000A;  an invisible hunting cloak&#x000A;  a black capsa (open)&#x000A;    a scroll of igram&#x000A;  a leather rucksack (open)&#x000A;    a blue capsa of mist (closed)&#x000A;    a red capsa of hasten (open)&#x000A;      a scroll of quiste&#x000A;    a purple capsa of opening (open)&#x000A;      a scroll of rezrov&#x000A;    a gold capsa of down (closed)&#x000A;&#x000A;Ash prattles happily, telling you about meeting a Throckwright, and getting to see his pouch of seeds.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You are carrying:&#x000A;  an invisible hunting cloak&#x000A;  a black capsa (open)&#x000A;    a scroll of igram&#x000A;  a leather rucksack (open)&#x000A;    a blue capsa of mist (closed)&#x000A;    a red capsa of hasten (open)&#x000A;      a scroll of quiste&#x000A;    a purple capsa of opening (open)&#x000A;      a scroll of rezrov&#x000A;    a gold capsa of down (closed)&#x000A;&#x000A;Ash prattles happily, telling you about meeting a Throckwright, and getting to see his pouch of seeds.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-267"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-267">
    <command xml:space="preserve">get capsa</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(the green capsa)&#x000A;You take a deep breath.  Once you take the green capsa, you'll be the "holder" of taclor, and Horatio will ask you for your decision.  Should you get it now?</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">(the green capsa)&#x000A;You take a deep breath.  Once you take the green capsa, you'll be the "holder" of taclor, and Horatio will ask you for your decision.  Should you get it now?</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-268"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-268">
    <command xml:space="preserve">y</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You're right.  It's time.&#x000A;&#x000A;You hold the capsa of health in your hands, turning it over and looking at it from all sides.  It's what you came here for.  To take it back home and save your mother.  Your people.  Is it still that simple?&#x000A;&#x000A;"You are now the holder of the scroll of taclor" says Horatio, as Ash continues to tell you about what it was like to see a real jaguar this one time.  "Will you have me read it?"&#x000A;&#x000A;1) "Ash was holding it before.  Why can't they make the decision?"&#x000A;2) "What will happen when you read it?"&#x000A;3) "Why not let the queen... let Aubrey decide?"&#x000A;4) Leave without the capsa.&#x000A;5) Leave with the capsa, and leave Ash behind.&#x000A;6) Leave with the capsa, and take Ash with you.&#x000A;7) Let Horatio read the scroll of taclor.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">You're right.  It's time.&#x000A;&#x000A;You hold the capsa of health in your hands, turning it over and looking at it from all sides.  It's what you came here for.  To take it back home and save your mother.  Your people.  Is it still that simple?&#x000A;&#x000A;"You are now the holder of the scroll of taclor" says Horatio, as Ash continues to tell you about what it was like to see a real jaguar this one time.  "Will you have me read it?"&#x000A;&#x000A;1) "Ash was holding it before.  Why can't they make the decision?"&#x000A;2) "What will happen when you read it?"&#x000A;3) "Why not let the queen... let Aubrey decide?"&#x000A;4) Leave without the capsa.&#x000A;5) Leave with the capsa, and leave Ash behind.&#x000A;6) Leave with the capsa, and take Ash with you.&#x000A;7) Let Horatio read the scroll of taclor.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-269"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-269">
    <command xml:space="preserve">1</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">["Ash was holding it before.  Why can't they make the decision?"]&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio looks at Ash, then looks at you.  Ash continues to tell you about having to get their desk grown twice in two months because they were growing so fast.&#x000A;&#x000A;Yeah, OK, fair.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio looks at you expectantly.&#x000A;&#x000A;1) "What will happen when you read it?"&#x000A;2) "Why not let the queen... let Aubrey decide?"&#x000A;3) Leave without the capsa.&#x000A;4) Leave with the capsa, and leave Ash behind.&#x000A;5) Leave with the capsa, and take Ash with you.&#x000A;6) Let Horatio read the scroll of taclor.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">["Ash was holding it before.  Why can't they make the decision?"]&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio looks at Ash, then looks at you.  Ash continues to tell you about having to get their desk grown twice in two months because they were growing so fast.&#x000A;&#x000A;Yeah, OK, fair.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio looks at you expectantly.&#x000A;&#x000A;1) "What will happen when you read it?"&#x000A;2) "Why not let the queen... let Aubrey decide?"&#x000A;3) Leave without the capsa.&#x000A;4) Leave with the capsa, and leave Ash behind.&#x000A;5) Leave with the capsa, and take Ash with you.&#x000A;6) Let Horatio read the scroll of taclor.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-270"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-270">
    <command xml:space="preserve">1</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">["What will happen when you read it?"]&#x000A;&#x000A;"I know not," Horatio replies.  "I know that it will grant a power related to the scroll's effect to some percentage of all people.  Everywhere.  Regardless of class or heritage or clan.  My guess is that it will improve their health--perhaps make them immune, perhaps give them regeneration, perhaps grant them an immortality, of sorts."&#x000A;&#x000A;"Will it affect people right now?" you ask, "Or just people in the future?  People hatched tomorrow?  Eggs laid tomorrow?"&#x000A;&#x000A;"The stories do not say," he replies.  "What difference is five years; twenty years to the march of history?"&#x000A;&#x000A;"It makes a difference to me," you say.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Indeed," he replies.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio looks at you expectantly.&#x000A;&#x000A;1) "Why not let the queen... let Aubrey decide?"&#x000A;2) Leave without the capsa.&#x000A;3) Leave with the capsa, and leave Ash behind.&#x000A;4) Leave with the capsa, and take Ash with you.&#x000A;5) Let Horatio read the scroll of taclor.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">["What will happen when you read it?"]&#x000A;&#x000A;"I know not," Horatio replies.  "I know that it will grant a power related to the scroll's effect to some percentage of all people.  Everywhere.  Regardless of class or heritage or clan.  My guess is that it will improve their health--perhaps make them immune, perhaps give them regeneration, perhaps grant them an immortality, of sorts."&#x000A;&#x000A;"Will it affect people right now?" you ask, "Or just people in the future?  People hatched tomorrow?  Eggs laid tomorrow?"&#x000A;&#x000A;"The stories do not say," he replies.  "What difference is five years; twenty years to the march of history?"&#x000A;&#x000A;"It makes a difference to me," you say.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Indeed," he replies.&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio looks at you expectantly.&#x000A;&#x000A;1) "Why not let the queen... let Aubrey decide?"&#x000A;2) Leave without the capsa.&#x000A;3) Leave with the capsa, and leave Ash behind.&#x000A;4) Leave with the capsa, and take Ash with you.&#x000A;5) Let Horatio read the scroll of taclor.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-271"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-271">
    <command xml:space="preserve">1</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">["Why not let the queen... let Aubrey decide?"]&#x000A;&#x000A;The feathers on Horatio's neck ruffle.  "She has already denied me.  Every day, I send a new request, and every day, she sends her rejection.  If you leave, I will keep asking her.  She may change her mind.  She may not.  You may know her better than I."&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio looks at you expectantly.&#x000A;&#x000A;1) Leave without the capsa.&#x000A;2) Leave with the capsa, and leave Ash behind.&#x000A;3) Leave with the capsa, and take Ash with you.&#x000A;4) Let Horatio read the scroll of taclor.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">["Why not let the queen... let Aubrey decide?"]&#x000A;&#x000A;The feathers on Horatio's neck ruffle.  "She has already denied me.  Every day, I send a new request, and every day, she sends her rejection.  If you leave, I will keep asking her.  She may change her mind.  She may not.  You may know her better than I."&#x000A;&#x000A;Horatio looks at you expectantly.&#x000A;&#x000A;1) Leave without the capsa.&#x000A;2) Leave with the capsa, and leave Ash behind.&#x000A;3) Leave with the capsa, and take Ash with you.&#x000A;4) Let Horatio read the scroll of taclor.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-272"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-272">
    <command xml:space="preserve">1</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">[Leave without the capsa.]&#x000A;&#x000A;Switching to Horatio.&#x000A;&#x000A;You watch as the struggle plays out across Constance's face, while Ash happily prattles behind her.  Slowly, she sets the capsa back down on the desk, and just stares at it.  "I can't do it," she finally says.  "I can't condemn Ash for the sake of my people.  I can't condemn anyone for the sake of a fairy-tale promise."&#x000A;&#x000A;1) Try to explain, again, that it's not a fairy tale.&#x000A;2) Let her process.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">[Leave without the capsa.]&#x000A;&#x000A;Switching to Horatio.&#x000A;&#x000A;You watch as the struggle plays out across Constance's face, while Ash happily prattles behind her.  Slowly, she sets the capsa back down on the desk, and just stares at it.  "I can't do it," she finally says.  "I can't condemn Ash for the sake of my people.  I can't condemn anyone for the sake of a fairy-tale promise."&#x000A;&#x000A;1) Try to explain, again, that it's not a fairy tale.&#x000A;2) Let her process.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-273"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-273">
    <command xml:space="preserve">1</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">[Try to explain, again, that it's not a fairy tale.]&#x000A;&#x000A;"It's no fairy tale," you say.  "It is my heritage.  I know---"&#x000A;&#x000A;Constance cuts you off.  "You don't know what will happen.  The fairy tale is that it will help me, today.  That it will help Ash.  That my mother--" her voice goes quiet, hoarse, "won't die."&#x000A;&#x000A;It's true. You hope things will get better, in the end.  You believe it, with all your being.  But you can't say anything about her people, or Ash.&#x000A;&#x000A;Constance reaches out a wing, and strokes Ash's head.  "I love you, kid," she tells them.  "Say hi to your mom for me."&#x000A;&#x000A;"You're not staying?" they ask, suddenly stricken.&#x000A;&#x000A;Constance shakes her head, steps onto the window ledge, and launches herself into the mist.  A keening cry from Ash, of confusion and loss.  You feel it as well, as you've felt it for years.  You had forgotten it could be given voice.&#x000A;&#x000A;As if summoned by the cry, the queen--Aubrey--rushes in, with her own cry of worry, replaced by one of relief.  She engulfs Ash in her wings.  "You're okay; you're okay," she repeats like a mantra, eyes closed, holding Ash tight.  She opens them to see taclor on the desk.  A questioning look at you.  "She didn't take it?  She didn't have you read it?"&#x000A;&#x000A;"No," you reply.  "She held it.  She could have done either."&#x000A;&#x000A;Aubrey breathes out and deflates.  The fight that sustained her for so long is over.  When your opponent concedes, victory in their grasp, what then?  You sense an opening.&#x000A;&#x000A;1) Ask her to let you read the scroll.&#x000A;2) Now is not the time.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">[Try to explain, again, that it's not a fairy tale.]&#x000A;&#x000A;"It's no fairy tale," you say.  "It is my heritage.  I know---"&#x000A;&#x000A;Constance cuts you off.  "You don't know what will happen.  The fairy tale is that it will help me, today.  That it will help Ash.  That my mother--" her voice goes quiet, hoarse, "won't die."&#x000A;&#x000A;It's true. You hope things will get better, in the end.  You believe it, with all your being.  But you can't say anything about her people, or Ash.&#x000A;&#x000A;Constance reaches out a wing, and strokes Ash's head.  "I love you, kid," she tells them.  "Say hi to your mom for me."&#x000A;&#x000A;"You're not staying?" they ask, suddenly stricken.&#x000A;&#x000A;Constance shakes her head, steps onto the window ledge, and launches herself into the mist.  A keening cry from Ash, of confusion and loss.  You feel it as well, as you've felt it for years.  You had forgotten it could be given voice.&#x000A;&#x000A;As if summoned by the cry, the queen--Aubrey--rushes in, with her own cry of worry, replaced by one of relief.  She engulfs Ash in her wings.  "You're okay; you're okay," she repeats like a mantra, eyes closed, holding Ash tight.  She opens them to see taclor on the desk.  A questioning look at you.  "She didn't take it?  She didn't have you read it?"&#x000A;&#x000A;"No," you reply.  "She held it.  She could have done either."&#x000A;&#x000A;Aubrey breathes out and deflates.  The fight that sustained her for so long is over.  When your opponent concedes, victory in their grasp, what then?  You sense an opening.&#x000A;&#x000A;1) Ask her to let you read the scroll.&#x000A;2) Now is not the time.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-274"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-274">
    <command xml:space="preserve">1</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">[Ask her to let you read the scroll.]&#x000A;&#x000A;"You are, once again, the holder of taclor," you say.  "Will you let me read it, and release its power to everyone, as the Gods intended?"&#x000A;&#x000A;Aubrey stares out at the impenetrable mist.  At nothing; at everything; at Constance.  She's actually considering the question, perhaps for the first time in years.  Ash looks up at her, a question and the beginnings of understanding on his face.  "Ask me again tomorrow," she finally says, eyes fixed on the mist; Ash under her wing.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Indeed," you reply.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;    *** The question is reconsidered. ***&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;Would you like to RESTART, RESTORE a saved game, QUIT, UNDO the last command, or get a list of the ACHIEVEMENTS you obtained?&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve">[Ask her to let you read the scroll.]&#x000A;&#x000A;"You are, once again, the holder of taclor," you say.  "Will you let me read it, and release its power to everyone, as the Gods intended?"&#x000A;&#x000A;Aubrey stares out at the impenetrable mist.  At nothing; at everything; at Constance.  She's actually considering the question, perhaps for the first time in years.  Ash looks up at her, a question and the beginnings of understanding on his face.  "Ask me again tomorrow," she finally says, eyes fixed on the mist; Ash under her wing.&#x000A;&#x000A;"Indeed," you reply.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;    *** The question is reconsidered. ***&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;Would you like to RESTART, RESTORE a saved game, QUIT, UNDO the last command, or get a list of the ACHIEVEMENTS you obtained?&#x000A;&gt;</commentary>
