  <item nodeId="node-449">
    <command xml:space="preserve">summon mist</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Calling on your heritage as a Bostrat, you sing the ancient song of mist and rain and thunder, summoning moisture from the air.  It slowly coalesces into a creeping grey mist, obscuring you from sight.  In gentler times, you would be doing this to ensure the growth of the fields and forests; now you must use it to hide from prying eyes that would keep you from your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;You stop at the natural inflection point for clouds given today's weather.  You could make it thicker still, though it would then start to dissipate.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-450"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-450">
    <command xml:space="preserve">d</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You descend in wide circles, pulling mist down with you in what you hope is a sufficiently unsuspicious manner, trusting your memorization of the air currents to tell you where you're going...&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-451"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-451">
    <command xml:space="preserve">d</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You tuck in your wings and dive down into the forest below the Aerie, dodging tightly-spaced trees with acrobatic precision.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the Forest&#x000A;The trees below the Royal Aerie grow more closely together than in the rest of the forest, and include a wider variety, so that differently-colored woods could be incorporated into the buildings above.  This makes it harder to navigate down here--or it would if you weren't so amazing at navigation.&#x000A;&#x000A;Even through the mist, your sharp eyes spot a fine net, stretched between the trees.  It seems to be set to prevent anyone from coming up from the forest below.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-452"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-452">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x net</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">A fine, strong net, stretched between and among the trees.  It wasn't here three days ago, which means they spent a lot of effort... to keep you on the Aerie-side of it.  You grin to yourself.&#x000A;&#x000A;The momentum you had from your dive wears off.  Fun while it lasted!&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-453"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-453">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x net</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">A fine, strong net, stretched between and among the trees.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-440">
    <command xml:space="preserve">test horatio_speedrun</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(Testing.)&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[1] summon mist&#x000A;Calling on your heritage as a Bostrat, you sing the ancient song of mist and rain and thunder, summoning moisture from the air.  It slowly coalesces into a creeping grey mist, obscuring you from sight.  In gentler times, you would be doing this to ensure the growth of the fields and forests; now you must use it to hide from prying eyes that would keep you from your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;You stop at the natural inflection point for clouds given today's weather.  You could make it thicker still, though it would then start to dissipate.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[2] d&#x000A;You descend in wide circles, pulling mist down with you in what you hope is a sufficiently unsuspicious manner, trusting your memorization of the air currents to tell you where you're going...&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[3] u&#x000A;&#x000A;High Above the Royal Aerie&#x000A;Your summoned mist both obscures you and blocks you from seeing the Royal Aerie.  But you've already memorized its layout,and how it relates to today's air currents, winds, and thermals.  Royal Quarters to the north and down, well defended by circling Raven clan guards.  The Librum to the east and down.  In the center of the Aerie (and directly below you) is the Great Hall.  Other royal aeries dot the forest in the distance, but this complex holds your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;You circle through the thin mist, observing but hidden from view.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[4] open purple&#x000A;You take a deep breath.  If you're going to get past any of the doors here, this is the only way.&#x000A;&#x000A;You open the purple capsa of opening, revealing a scroll of rezrov.&#x000A;&#x000A;As you open the purple capsa, an almost-palpable wave of force emanates from it, as the power of the revealed scroll of rezrov is released.&#x000A;&#x000A;The magic of the gold capsa of down prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The magic of the red capsa of hasten prevents it from being opened.&#x000A;The straps and buckles on your rucksack fly open and it falls!&#x000A;&#x000A;The leather rucksack twists away as it falls below you, towards the Great Hall.&#x000A;&#x000A;From... well, from everywhere in the Aerie, it seems, Woodpeckers start drumming out messages in their Pounding dialect:  "Intruder! Estimated direction is..." and then each one individually seems to be telegraphing the direction from them to you.  You can't discern any one drummer from any other drummer, but you can at least tell that each seems to be drumming on sheets of metal that differ from each other, so every frequency is unique.  That makes the information somewhat useless to you, because you've not been trained to distinguish Pounding at different frequencies.  And because you already know where you are.  Sadly, the Raven Guards are indeed trained to distinguish Pounding frequencies.&#x000A;&#x000A;And if they didn't know where you were, they do now.&#x000A;&#x000A;You suddenly feel warmer, and hear an exultant song of the sun in the distance.  The queen must have Ikniq working for her, trained to try to burn away your fog.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[5] d&#x000A;You tuck in your wings and dive down towards the Aerie, thrilling to the misty wind streaming through your feathers.&#x000A;&#x000A;Great Hall Landing Cradle&#x000A;The Landing Cradle of the Great Hall spreads out over nearly a quarter of the vast building.  During your time here, you learned this was so that when a number of important guests and their retinues arrive at the same time, they can land simultaneously, instead of one after the other, which some would invariably take as meaning "in order of importance".&#x000A;&#x000A;The huge double doors of the Great Hall are on the west side of the landing cradle, and unguarded.  To the north is the Royal Quarters and Gardens, the Librum to the east, and as always, you can return to the skies or descend to the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;You can see a leather rucksack (in which are a purple capsa of opening (in which is a scroll of rezrov), a gold capsa of down (closed), and a red capsa of hasten (closed)) here.&#x000A;&#x000A;You've dived straight into a squad of Raven Guards, on their way up to accost you.  Fortunately, your speed helped you avoid most of them, but one guard's talon catches you on your side as you twist by them.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;[6] d&#x000A;&#x000A;In the Forest&#x000A;The trees below the Royal Aerie grow more closely together than in the rest of the forest, and include a wider variety, so that differently-colored woods could be incorporated into the buildings above.  This makes it harder to navigate down here--or it would if you weren't so amazing at navigation.&#x000A;&#x000A;Even through the mist, your sharp eyes spot a fine net, stretched between the trees.  It seems to be set to prevent anyone from coming up from the forest below.&#x000A;&#x000A;You expertly twist at breakneck speeds, weaving through three Ash trunks, over a branch, and around and behind a Redwood, where you halt, twist, and dive straight down the trunk, out of view of any stray Raven.&#x000A;&#x000A;The Raven's frustrated caws echo in the thin mist.  In time, the woodpeckers cease their drumming, and the cawing fades as well.  Protocol would dictate that they return to guarding priority items.  If there were any reserves left, they would be called up, but the Red Plague has affected the Raven Guard as sorely as your own community.&#x000A;&#x000A;You retrieve your rucksack and any fallen capsae, and plot a now-unseen course back to the familiar currents above the Aerie to ponder your next move.&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;&#x000A;                                                              *    *    *</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-441"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-441">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You wait, expectantly.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-442"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-442">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Silently, your cell door unlocks, then swings open.</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-443"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-443">
    <command xml:space="preserve"> </command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Well above your cell, you sense quiste, rezrov, rudenj, and quiste settle in their movements until they make lazy circles, high above the Aerie. Igram and taclor remain in place, quiet.&#x000A;&#x000A;It is time.&#x000A;&#x000A;Forgotten Brig&#x000A;A small but cosy cell, grown with austerity but basic comfort in mind.  Your now-open cell door leads west.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-444"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-444">
    <command xml:space="preserve">open blue</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You open the blue capsa of mist, revealing a scroll of bostrat.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-445"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-445">
    <command xml:space="preserve">close blue</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You close the blue capsa of mist.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-446"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-446">
    <command xml:space="preserve">drop blue</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The queen and her advisors were unimpressed by the capsa, dismissing it as an obvious fake.  But you think you can use it to convince Constance.  Better hang on to it.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-447"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-447">
    <command xml:space="preserve">w</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Disused Hallway&#x000A;The only time you ever saw anyone in this hallway was when Georg came to give you your meals, or clean the cell.  The living walls, still elegantly patterned, even here, self-replenish, and the floor carries away shed bark through the grate.  It leads west into the living area, and your old cell door leads east.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-448"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-448">
    <command xml:space="preserve">d</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You flatten yourself to the floor and, hearing your bones creak, roll into the space behind the grate.  Using your minimal throck ability, you whisper a song to the veins of this place: "I am extra.  I am not needed.  Take me from this place, which will renew itself through my absence."&#x000A;&#x000A;After a few moments, you feel an undulation in the slick rippled floor beneath you, and you are compressed even further, as its peristalsis slides you slowly, and then more rapidly, away from your only home for the last ten years.  Then with a sudden &gt;plop&lt;, you're ejected into space.&#x000A;&#x000A;You try to spread your wings, but your reaction time is not what it was, and you hit wirey netting before fully stopping yourself.&#x000A;&#x000A;No matter.&#x000A;&#x000A;In the Forest&#x000A;The tightly-growing trees and thick fog surround you tightly.  It would be oppressive, but for the echo of the Throckwright song you can just sense, flowing through the veins of these trees still.  That, and the fact that you've been confined to a single room for a decade, so any contrast is welcome.&#x000A;&#x000A;The net that caught you stretches in every direction, preventing both entrance to and egress from the rest of the forest.&#x000A;&#x000A;A thick mist surrounds you, summoned by your quarry.&#x000A;&#x000A;&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <changed>NO</changed>
  </item>
</Skein>
